1
00:00:40,031 --> 00:00:47,276
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if we continue by ānāpānasati, following from the previous discussion.

2
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:55,561
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you breathe?

3
00:01:02,565 --> 00:01:03,286
[SPEAKER_00]: How are you doing that?

4
00:01:22,275 --> 00:01:23,916
[SPEAKER_03]: You inhale and then you exhale.

5
00:01:24,176 --> 00:01:24,996
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you inhale?

6
00:01:25,116 --> 00:01:25,936
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you exhale?

7
00:01:28,417 --> 00:01:29,318
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you lift your arms?

8
00:01:30,838 --> 00:01:31,559
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you stand up?

9
00:01:31,859 --> 00:01:32,639
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you sit down?

10
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,061
[SPEAKER_01]: You intend to do it.

11
00:01:37,921 --> 00:01:38,821
[SPEAKER_01]: You intend to do it.

12
00:01:39,441 --> 00:01:39,662
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

13
00:01:40,222 --> 00:01:43,363
[SPEAKER_01]: But is there anything in between the intention and the action of doing it?

14
00:01:49,665 --> 00:01:51,346
[SPEAKER_01]: How does that... does that intention...

15
00:01:53,215 --> 00:01:54,135
[SPEAKER_01]: Where does that intention go?

16
00:01:55,216 --> 00:01:56,816
[SPEAKER_01]: Does it enter the body and move your arm?

17
00:01:58,837 --> 00:02:00,918
[SPEAKER_01]: Does it intend to breathe and breathe out?

18
00:02:03,999 --> 00:02:04,699
[SPEAKER_01]: Where is the intention?

19
00:02:04,759 --> 00:02:05,299
[SPEAKER_01]: Where is the body?

20
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,460
[SPEAKER_01]: Where is the breath, in this case?

21
00:02:09,141 --> 00:02:10,221
[SPEAKER_01]: You know the answer.

22
00:02:10,241 --> 00:02:15,743
[SPEAKER_01]: We'll be talking about it in some other video.

23
00:02:30,103 --> 00:02:30,483
[SPEAKER_01]: Breathing.

24
00:02:31,124 --> 00:02:32,225
[SPEAKER_01]: Take a long breath.

25
00:02:33,706 --> 00:02:34,587
[SPEAKER_01]: Take a short breath.

26
00:02:34,647 --> 00:02:35,767
[SPEAKER_01]: Take a forceful breath.

27
00:02:35,988 --> 00:02:41,212
[SPEAKER_01]: Take a light breath.

28
00:02:41,232 --> 00:02:41,992
[SPEAKER_01]: Where's the intention?

29
00:02:42,032 --> 00:02:42,713
[SPEAKER_01]: Where's the breathing?

30
00:02:45,575 --> 00:02:48,377
[SPEAKER_02]: I'd say the intention is underneath.

31
00:02:56,123 --> 00:02:56,704
[SPEAKER_01]: But is it, though?

32
00:02:59,007 --> 00:03:02,128
[SPEAKER_01]: That's exactly how you would start, but is it underneath?

33
00:03:03,428 --> 00:03:03,968
[SPEAKER_01]: Underneath what?

34
00:03:08,770 --> 00:03:09,970
[SPEAKER_01]: Underneath the breath.

35
00:03:11,930 --> 00:03:13,411
[SPEAKER_01]: But what is that intention when you look at it?

36
00:03:15,971 --> 00:03:17,612
[SPEAKER_01]: It's an image of the physical breathing.

37
00:03:22,893 --> 00:03:26,194
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if there is no image of the physical breathing, there'll be no intention.

38
00:03:34,043 --> 00:03:35,869
[SPEAKER_01]: So, why does it feel like underneath that?

39
00:03:39,341 --> 00:03:39,863
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it does.

40
00:04:28,603 --> 00:04:33,226
[SPEAKER_00]: Because of the assumption of there being a relationship between the intention and...

41
00:04:33,827 --> 00:04:34,027
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

42
00:04:35,188 --> 00:04:38,931
[SPEAKER_01]: But there is a relationship, so... You start with a relationship.

43
00:04:39,831 --> 00:04:42,333
[SPEAKER_01]: That's obviously wrongly assumed.

44
00:04:43,774 --> 00:04:46,716
[SPEAKER_01]: But can people tell the details about that wrong assumption?

45
00:04:47,237 --> 00:04:47,837
[SPEAKER_01]: Particulars?

46
00:04:54,302 --> 00:04:55,383
[SPEAKER_03]: Is this what, eh...

47
00:04:57,166 --> 00:05:24,506
[SPEAKER_03]: I mean, this is, I think, what I meant when we were talking last time, when I said there's like this kind of blurring of boundaries between the the intention to breathe that kind of makes the body do the breathing, and then you feel the body breathing, and you feel like you have... or the intention has caused the breathing.

48
00:05:24,526 --> 00:05:25,467
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, yes.

49
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:26,948
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's obviously not something

50
00:05:27,544 --> 00:05:33,010
[SPEAKER_03]: You're actively thinking, but it is implied in every bodily action.

51
00:05:33,050 --> 00:05:45,424
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it's implied, for example, through regarding your intention as something under the breath, that already carries that overlap that cannot be.

52
00:05:45,984 --> 00:05:47,126
[SPEAKER_01]: Overlap of the domains.

53
00:05:48,570 --> 00:05:49,670
[SPEAKER_03]: But you start with that.

54
00:05:49,871 --> 00:05:50,831
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to start with that.

55
00:05:50,931 --> 00:05:56,353
[SPEAKER_01]: You start with what it actually... And even if somebody describes a difference, I might say, oh, I don't feel like it's on there.

56
00:05:56,373 --> 00:05:57,314
[SPEAKER_01]: I feel like it's in here.

57
00:05:57,654 --> 00:06:07,358
[SPEAKER_01]: Either way, see, you realize any positionality, so to speak, in regard to the breath, assumes a relationship with it.

58
00:06:08,798 --> 00:06:08,978
Yeah.

59
00:06:11,459 --> 00:06:11,660
[SPEAKER_03]: But...

60
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:16,942
[SPEAKER_01]: Assumes breath to come out of the intention.

61
00:06:18,729 --> 00:06:31,915
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in other words, your intention, gratuitously, not knowing that it's actually impossible, takes up the body, presuming it's breathing, so to speak.

62
00:06:32,375 --> 00:06:38,078
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, your thoughts take up your mouth when you speak.

63
00:06:38,098 --> 00:06:48,043
[SPEAKER_01]: Because when you think, and you say what you think, the implicit assumption is that it's those thoughts have become these words, have descended

64
00:06:48,925 --> 00:06:57,732
[SPEAKER_01]: And turned into the sounds, there's this, as I said, kind of directionality from you outward, and same with the breath.

65
00:06:58,913 --> 00:07:01,735
[SPEAKER_01]: But actually, there... well, that's impossible.

66
00:07:02,835 --> 00:07:15,365
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the whole point of the practice, is to completely remove any traces of that directionality that implies ownership, and me here, doing these things through the body, through the speech, through the mental intentions.

67
00:07:20,930 --> 00:07:21,871
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how do you then breathe?

68
00:07:22,591 --> 00:07:34,479
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if the intention is not actually... cannot actually descend into the physical domain, cannot actually take it up, how do you breathe?

69
00:07:38,202 --> 00:07:39,663
[SPEAKER_01]: How can you not forget to breathe?

70
00:07:41,604 --> 00:07:44,326
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, you can forget about breathing, but you never forget to breathe.

71
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:46,408
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not that you are doing it.

72
00:07:46,548 --> 00:07:47,769
[SPEAKER_01]: It is happening.

73
00:07:48,769 --> 00:07:49,650
[SPEAKER_01]: So, who's doing it then?

74
00:08:00,755 --> 00:08:02,315
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it's not you who's doing it.

75
00:08:03,256 --> 00:08:04,076
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't be doing it.

76
00:08:04,736 --> 00:08:06,257
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're asking who's doing it, is it?

77
00:08:06,317 --> 00:08:07,957
[SPEAKER_01]: So, who or what is doing it?

78
00:08:09,618 --> 00:08:12,098
[SPEAKER_00]: It's unavoidably there.

79
00:08:12,199 --> 00:08:13,039
[SPEAKER_00]: Something is doing it.

80
00:08:13,459 --> 00:08:15,339
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, intention is doing it, which is unavoidable.

81
00:08:15,359 --> 00:08:15,600
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it?

82
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:15,800
[SPEAKER_00]: How?

83
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:17,660
[SPEAKER_01]: How can intention be there?

84
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:18,520
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, sorry, the body, sorry.

85
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:18,941
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, there's no...

86
00:08:18,961 --> 00:08:19,221
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

87
00:08:19,241 --> 00:08:19,681
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, the body.

88
00:08:19,841 --> 00:08:20,921
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the body is doing it.

89
00:08:22,822 --> 00:08:24,062
[SPEAKER_01]: In its bodily domain.

90
00:08:26,043 --> 00:08:30,004
[SPEAKER_01]: On account of your intention, in its intentional domain,

91
00:08:31,178 --> 00:08:33,120
[SPEAKER_03]: It's even that that goes...

92
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:37,703
[SPEAKER_03]: I'm thinking, if I say the body is doing it...

93
00:08:37,763 --> 00:08:42,187
[SPEAKER_01]: If you just say the body is doing it, then, obviously, it can be misunderstood.

94
00:08:43,348 --> 00:08:48,132
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you say it at the end of all this questioning, then it's hopefully clear what we mean by that.

95
00:08:49,593 --> 00:08:54,037
[SPEAKER_01]: So, presence of intention makes the body breathe.

96
00:08:56,699 --> 00:08:58,120
[SPEAKER_01]: But there's no relationship between the two.

97
00:08:59,321 --> 00:09:00,622
[SPEAKER_01]: Those two domains don't connect.

98
00:09:01,067 --> 00:09:08,369
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no live wire that connects the intentional domain and touches the body and then snaps it into breathing.

99
00:09:08,689 --> 00:09:13,130
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just intention to breathe is here and body breathing is here.

100
00:09:16,071 --> 00:09:16,911
[SPEAKER_00]: And there's nothing in between.

101
00:09:18,911 --> 00:09:25,673
[SPEAKER_01]: There's no directionality, overlap, connection in between.

102
00:09:25,973 --> 00:09:26,253
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just

103
00:09:27,192 --> 00:09:30,995
[SPEAKER_01]: Your intention to breathe exists in its own domain, directed in its own direction.

104
00:09:31,896 --> 00:09:35,539
[SPEAKER_01]: Simultaneous to that, there is the body corresponding to it.

105
00:09:35,559 --> 00:09:37,861
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the relationship...

106
00:09:41,083 --> 00:09:44,906
[SPEAKER_01]: If there were to be a relationship, it's inconceivable by you.

107
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:48,589
[SPEAKER_01]: You were let out from that relationship.

108
00:09:51,592 --> 00:09:56,516
[SPEAKER_01]: But see, even thinking that there is an external relationship between them, that I'm not privy to,

109
00:09:57,395 --> 00:09:58,475
[SPEAKER_01]: can become your assumption.

110
00:09:59,716 --> 00:10:16,162
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's really the only way to reach the point of not assuming the impossible relationship between the two internally, is to undo any notion, tacit assumptions of overlap, of directionality.

111
00:10:16,323 --> 00:10:17,343
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, what's left?

112
00:10:18,583 --> 00:10:22,425
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, is the conscious body in name and form, externally.

113
00:10:25,092 --> 00:10:29,155
[SPEAKER_01]: The domain of the breathing body and everything else, external name and form.

114
00:10:35,818 --> 00:10:37,840
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's really the training of ānāpānasati.

115
00:10:40,321 --> 00:10:49,086
[SPEAKER_01]: It's undermined at very first, very subtle, very easily done, because it's already a starting point, connection between

116
00:10:50,327 --> 00:10:56,110
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the whole point of the intentional, those steps in ānāpānasati, where you're intentionally breathing like this or like that.

117
00:10:56,951 --> 00:11:00,112
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not shying away from intentional involvement with the breath.

118
00:11:00,312 --> 00:11:04,475
[SPEAKER_01]: Once, obviously, the proper mind recollectedness and knowledge of the breath is established.

119
00:11:05,255 --> 00:11:06,996
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you want to hammer it in.

120
00:11:07,616 --> 00:11:16,321
[SPEAKER_01]: That no matter how forceful, how determined, how intentional your intention is, it remains fully enclosed within its own domain.

121
00:11:17,281 --> 00:11:18,702
[SPEAKER_01]: And the body doesn't even know about it.

122
00:11:20,299 --> 00:11:23,061
[SPEAKER_01]: But look, it's happening because of the intention.

123
00:11:23,801 --> 00:11:25,562
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yes, that still doesn't mean they connect.

124
00:11:26,783 --> 00:11:29,364
[SPEAKER_01]: Not in any measurable way by you internally.

125
00:11:46,574 --> 00:11:48,995
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you stretch the same principle.

126
00:11:51,912 --> 00:12:02,996
[SPEAKER_01]: And actually, once you start undoing or seeing through the gratuitous assumption of this directionality, from my intention the breath comes, you realize the breathing is always underneath.

127
00:12:03,496 --> 00:12:05,937
[SPEAKER_01]: The body, the domain of the body is always underneath.

128
00:12:06,957 --> 00:12:13,879
[SPEAKER_01]: Underneath your domain of intentions, underneath the domain of your feelings, underneath the domain of your mind.

129
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:15,680
[SPEAKER_01]: Citta.

130
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:19,461
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly why you start stretching the same principle.

131
00:12:21,825 --> 00:12:24,107
[SPEAKER_01]: Breathing in like this, I'll experience the body.

132
00:12:24,167 --> 00:12:27,369
[SPEAKER_01]: Breathing in like this, breathing out like this, I'll experience the feeling.

133
00:12:27,509 --> 00:12:29,350
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll experience the mind.

134
00:12:29,370 --> 00:12:32,092
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll experience the dhammas, the images.

135
00:12:34,614 --> 00:12:51,345
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if the body is inaccessible, underneath, and the correspondence of bodily actions and presence of mental reactions has no measurable directionality, overlap, connection, not even a trace,

136
00:12:52,723 --> 00:12:59,647
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, there's absolutely... in the very core, there is nothing that you can deem, yeah, but this came from me.

137
00:13:01,608 --> 00:13:03,108
[SPEAKER_01]: This has originated from me.

138
00:13:07,210 --> 00:13:10,052
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it completely undermines the perception of any mastery.

139
00:13:11,313 --> 00:13:15,935
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you realize, even when I intend, I only know it worked because the body over there

140
00:13:16,726 --> 00:13:17,547
[SPEAKER_01]: You breathe into it.

141
00:13:17,607 --> 00:13:18,827
[SPEAKER_03]: Happened to do it, basically.

142
00:13:19,027 --> 00:13:20,528
[SPEAKER_01]: Happened to do it to an account of this.

143
00:13:20,908 --> 00:13:25,111
[SPEAKER_03]: And even that, you only kind of know indirectly, like, as in, you have to... Yeah.

144
00:13:25,771 --> 00:13:26,412
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

145
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:27,772
[SPEAKER_03]: Even that, it's underneath.

146
00:13:27,852 --> 00:13:29,733
[SPEAKER_03]: It's kind of underneath that.

147
00:13:30,434 --> 00:13:31,074
[SPEAKER_03]: That's the point.

148
00:13:31,414 --> 00:13:37,338
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly why, well, at some point, you will stop breathing, despite how strong you will intend to breathe.

149
00:13:38,118 --> 00:13:38,979
[SPEAKER_01]: You will not be able to.

150
00:13:40,019 --> 00:13:41,700
[SPEAKER_03]: I was gonna say, actually, because those...

151
00:13:42,821 --> 00:13:44,322
[SPEAKER_03]: This is something I was thinking about, like,

152
00:13:49,666 --> 00:13:50,507
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't know how to put this.

153
00:13:50,527 --> 00:14:14,290
[SPEAKER_03]: Okay, so, let's say with speaking, like, it's very, it's quite clear that at the moment when I speak, when I actually speak, I can only do it by kind of looking past the actual thoughts.

154
00:14:15,717 --> 00:14:22,442
[SPEAKER_03]: And I was starting to notice that there is... it feels like there's a corresponding thing with the intention to breathe.

155
00:14:22,622 --> 00:14:26,824
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, if I actually become... if I'm very aware... Well, that's what you're training against.

156
00:14:27,985 --> 00:14:30,007
[SPEAKER_01]: Your training is supposed to undo that.

157
00:14:31,848 --> 00:14:37,151
[SPEAKER_01]: That... because, yes, of course, every intentional involvement will make you look past the intentional to the thing.

158
00:14:37,551 --> 00:14:44,356
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why it just naturally leads to that assumption of the physicality, the connection with it, that whole...

159
00:14:45,865 --> 00:14:53,047
[SPEAKER_01]: Proliferation that takes place on account of simply not knowing that those things are not connectable.

160
00:14:56,588 --> 00:15:13,452
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's like developing the perception of that... well, developing the practice, say, of the intentional breathing, whereby intention does not spill out into the juxtaposed physical domain that exists in its own extent.

161
00:15:13,472 --> 00:15:13,712
[SPEAKER_01]: Then,

162
00:15:14,342 --> 00:15:24,186
[SPEAKER_01]: The perceptions of that physical domain that exists in, in some extent, you use to undermine any other intentional involvement, not necessarily in regard to breathing.

163
00:15:24,966 --> 00:15:33,429
[SPEAKER_01]: In regard to any feeling that's present, in regard to any mind state, in regard to any pressure, there is the body breathing underneath it.

164
00:15:34,930 --> 00:15:42,513
[SPEAKER_01]: And just to the extent that you know that correctly, to that extent, the domain that's pressuring you to take up the directionality,

165
00:15:43,549 --> 00:15:47,371
[SPEAKER_01]: To follow it, it's kind of frozen, so to speak.

166
00:15:47,431 --> 00:15:48,852
[SPEAKER_01]: You freeze it in its own extent.

167
00:15:50,233 --> 00:15:53,695
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if the pressure remains within it, you are not the one pressured.

168
00:16:02,241 --> 00:16:13,288
[SPEAKER_01]: So, practicing in regard to these four things, there'll be nothing... well, there'll be no more... there'll be no place left for any assumed overlaps and connections to exist.

169
00:16:14,616 --> 00:16:16,137
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it would be like that simile in the suttas.

170
00:16:16,817 --> 00:16:29,606
[SPEAKER_01]: A skilled monk is like a butcher that cuts up a cow and completely, clearly, fully separates, piles its meat, tendon, bones, organs, clearly.

171
00:16:29,626 --> 00:16:38,272
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize, oh, yeah, they were piled up together, but they were never one with each other or blending one into another.

172
00:16:38,852 --> 00:16:41,554
[SPEAKER_01]: Always clearly separate things.

173
00:16:43,225 --> 00:16:49,630
[SPEAKER_01]: Obviously, people often misunderstand that as some sort of dry intellectual analysis of elements.

174
00:16:50,290 --> 00:16:53,633
[SPEAKER_01]: But, if you approach it phenomenologically, you realize, no, those domains are phenomena.

175
00:16:55,354 --> 00:17:02,740
[SPEAKER_01]: They're aggregates of phenomena, and you see them in its own extent, in its full extent, completely independent of each other.

176
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:04,621
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why it's the five heaps.

177
00:17:05,902 --> 00:17:06,523
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not one heap.

178
00:17:07,804 --> 00:17:10,446
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter how much it's heaped up, you will always discern.

179
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:16,283
[SPEAKER_01]: rūpa, vedanā, sañña, sankhāra, viññāṇa.

180
00:17:20,386 --> 00:17:26,251
[SPEAKER_01]: And anything in this layer that belongs to sañña, goes to sañña.

181
00:17:26,391 --> 00:17:28,213
[SPEAKER_01]: It's understood under a sañña domain.

182
00:17:29,554 --> 00:17:32,596
[SPEAKER_01]: Anything belongs under vedanā, it's understood under vedanā domain.

183
00:17:33,617 --> 00:17:34,778
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter the specifics.

184
00:17:44,597 --> 00:18:05,325
[SPEAKER_01]: You're intentionally breathing differently, long, short, knowingly, but not for the sake of breathing, but for the sake of fully, kind of, dragging out an implicit assumption that at least some degree of your intentionality flows into the physical and makes you breathe.

185
00:18:19,258 --> 00:18:24,943
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the result of that is a perception of complete, utter confinement.

186
00:18:27,205 --> 00:18:35,131
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not as unpleasant as if it were to be discovered through the contemplation of death or a subha.

187
00:18:36,893 --> 00:18:41,476
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that body, that domain of body breathing there, always has been like that.

188
00:18:43,038 --> 00:18:45,820
[SPEAKER_01]: Independent of you, having a life of its own, so to speak.

189
00:18:47,561 --> 00:18:48,382
[SPEAKER_01]: Neither good nor bad.

190
00:18:49,642 --> 00:18:51,523
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, ah, it's fairly neutral.

191
00:18:52,804 --> 00:18:59,089
[SPEAKER_01]: So, although you're completely confined within it, you realize you're confined within the neutrality, and that's not a problem, really.

192
00:19:05,173 --> 00:19:17,802
